WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.480
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.680
Today we continue
our series on Ozempic

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.440
as we look at the potential side
effects of GLP-1 weight-loss drugs,

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.480
such as suicide, pancreatitis,
bowel obstruction,

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.600
thyroid cancer,
and pancreatic cancer.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.840
GLP-1 weight-loss drugs.
How safe are they?

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.080
Regulatory authorities
have expressed concerns

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.520
about the potential risk
of acute pancreatitis,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.160
thyroid cancer,
and kidney failure,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.760
warnings that are
appropriately conveyed

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.160
in every box of drugs
handed to a patient.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.720
Here’s the actual package insert
for high-dose Ozempic,

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.800
sold for weight loss as Wegovy.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.480
Warnings and precautions
include thyroid tumors,

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.000
acute inflammation
of the pancreas,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.280
acute gallbladder disease,

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.800
heightened risk
of low blood sugars

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.960
if you’re on blood
sugar-lowering medications,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.440
acute kidney injury,
allergic reactions,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.080
worsening eye disease
for those with type 2 diabetes,

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.320
an increase in heart rate
that should be monitored,

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.880
and suicidal thoughts
and behaviors.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:13.920
And the package insert

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.080
for the other major
GLP-1 weight loss drug,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.080
tirzepatide, sold as Zepbound,

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.880
reads almost word for word
the same.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.040
Let’s start with the good news,
suicide.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.800
The possibility of an adverse
psychiatric event on GLP-1 drugs

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.400
is biologically plausible

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.040
because GLP-1 receptors
are widely expressed

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.840
in the central nervous system,
including our brain.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.800
So, what does the science show?

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.200
This meta-analysis
of randomized controlled trials

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.200
did not highlight
any detrimental effect

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.560
on these drugs on mental health,
including suicide.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.800
Now, this meta-analysis
only covered studies

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.920
up through the end of 2023
and only clinical trials,

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.680
and those with mental illnesses

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.160
are usually excluded
from such studies.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.680
But there have been
newer studies done

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.360
with subjects
out in the real world,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.080
and again,
no clear increased risk.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.600
And this study,
on the association

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.360
of the Ozempic drug semaglutide

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.320
with risk of suicidal ideation
in another cohort

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.840
found that the drug
was associated

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.040
with a lower risk

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.760
for incident and recurrent
suicidal ideation,

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.440
apparently cutting
suicidal thoughts

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.200
by more than half,
compared to those

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.240
on the older, less effective
weight-loss drugs.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.080
After all,
a weight-reducing treatment

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.760
that limits
the burden of obesity

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.760
could improve mood.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.280
I told you suicide
was the good news!

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.720
Now, on to cancer.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.240
Both Wegovy, high-dose Ozempic,
and Zepbound (tirzepatide),

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.480
carry so-called
black box warnings

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.560
for thyroid cancer risk.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.440
Black box warnings

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.520
are the U.S. Food
and Drug Administration’s

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.480
strictest caution

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.200
about potentially
life-threatening hazards.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.680
In rodents, these drugs
cause dose-dependent

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.000
and duration-dependent
thyroid tumors

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.920
at clinically relevant
exposures,

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.400
meaning the kind of doses
prescribed to humans.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.720
Now, we don’t know yet
whether these drugs cause

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.080
a thyroid cancer called
medullary thyroid carcinoma,

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.280
which is a cancer of
the thyroid C cells in humans.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.240
To be on the safe side,

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.920
the drugs shouldn’t
be prescribed

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.120
for high-risk individuals,

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.200
like those with a personal
or family history

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.880
of thyroid cancer,

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.360
but it’s not like the rats
had thyroid cancer

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.200
running in their families.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.880
Doctors should counsel
their patients

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.920
to remain alert
for symptoms of thyroid tumors,

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.680
like a lump
or swelling in the neck,

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.680
trouble swallowing,
shortness of breath,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.080
or persistent hoarseness.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.560
I’d be curious in the comments
to see if any viewers

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.840
who’ve been prescribed
these drugs

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:35.360
were told any of this
by their prescribing physicians.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.120
Can’t we just ultrasound
people’s necks

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.080
to see if they develop
thyroid tumors on these drugs?

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.160
That’s considered to be
of uncertain value,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:45.040
since no such studies
have been done.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.960
Now, there have been
studies done

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.800
on GLP-1 drugs, like Ozempic,

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.138
and the risk of thyroid cancer
in people.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.240
Researchers found increased risk
of all thyroid cancers

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.400
and specifically,
medullary thyroid cancer

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.320
in people using these drugs,

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.800
particularly after taking them
for a few years.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.840
A commentary
citing the study asked,

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.160
"Is it the time
to be concerned?"

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.480
Maybe that one study
was just a fluke?

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.800
No, after putting together
all the best studies,

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.640
a systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.040
of randomized controlled trials
found, again,

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.200
a significant increase
in the risk

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.040
of overall thyroid cancer,
about 52 percent greater odds.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.600
That sounds bad,
until you realize

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:26.640
just how rare
the cancer is overall.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.520
The incidence of thyroid cancer
in this kind of population

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:34.320
is 0.285 cases
per 1,000 patient years.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.560
This means that
over a span of 10 years,

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.280
we’d only expect
about three people out of 1,000

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.720
to get that cancer.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.760
So, even if you bump up
that risk by 50 percent,

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.800
you’re still only talking
about four in 1,000

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.440
getting it over a decade,
compared to three in 1,000

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.680
if you hadn’t started
taking the drugs.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.920
That translates to a five-year
"number needed to harm"

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.240
of 1,349.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:01.280
That means that even if this
were truly cause-and-effect,

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:05.280
it would take treating
1,349 people for five years

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.800
to cause a single additional
case of thyroid cancer.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.080
And even if you’re
the unlucky soul who gets it,

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.400
it’s pretty mild, as cancers go.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.240
The five-year
relative survival rate,

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.640
meaning the likelihood
you’ll still be alive

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.240
five years after diagnosis

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.760
compared to people
without the cancer

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:24.240
is 98.4 percent.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:27.040
Okay, but what about the risk
of pancreatic cancer

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.560
with the use of these drugs?

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.560
That has a relative
five-year survival rate

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:33.687
of only 12.8 percent.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.200
For thyroid cancer,

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.880
a bunch of people are
diagnosed with it,

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.960
but very few die from it,

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.480
whereas for pancreatic cancer,

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:43.120
almost everyone who gets it
dies from it.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:46.000
So, do these drugs cause
pancreatic cancer?

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.920
That’s exactly the question
I’ll address next.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.680
The most common
adverse side effects

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.440
of Ozempic-type
weight-loss drugs

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.840
are gastrointestinal issues,

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:59.680
including nausea, vomiting,
diarrhea, and constipation,

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.960
but Ozempic may also heighten
the risk of pancreatitis,

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.760
kidney failure,
and thyroid cancer.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.880
Many of the kidney issues
may stem from dehydration

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.960
due to excessive vomiting
or diarrhea

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.240
caused by the drugs,

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.800
but what
about the pancreas inflammation?

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.640
Analyzing
the prescription records

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.880
of 16 million Americans,

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.800
compared to taking
an older class

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.160
of weight-loss drugs,

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.640
the use of GLP-1 drugs
like Ozempic

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:28.640
was associated with nine times
more pancreatitis,

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:30.080
as well as four times
higher risk

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.000
of bowel obstruction.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.280
Remember, GLP-1 slows down
your digestive tract.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.240
That’s part of the reason
people get nauseous and barfy,

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.560
but that’s also part of why
you feel fuller for longer

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.000
and lose weight.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.480
But sometimes, it can
make your gut so sluggish,

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.560
it stops working,
and you get a blockage

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:49.120
that could become
a surgical emergency.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:51.040
It’s super rare, though.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:56.000
The number needed to harm
after one year of use is 1,223,

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.600
meaning that
more than 1,000 people

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.200
would have to take the drug
for a year

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:02.320
to cause a single extra case
of bowel obstruction.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.080
So, even after 10 years
of treatment,

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:07.200
your cumulative risk
would be less than one percent.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:11.200
But what about this 800 percent
increased risk of pancreatitis?

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.720
Digestive hormones like GLP-1
act on multiple targets

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:17.120
within the body,
with multiple effects,

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.800
perhaps more "magic shotgun"
than "magic bullet,"

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:24.000
but maybe not so magical
for the pancreas.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.640
GLP-1 receptors are
expressed abundantly

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:27.840
throughout the pancreas,

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.400
and in response
to GLP-1 therapy,

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.480
the cells of the pancreas
proliferate,

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:33.520
swelling the organ

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:36.080
and potentially
squeezing off ducts,

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:39.200
causing inflammation,
at least in rats,

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:41.440
but that led to human studies
like this,

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.960
suggesting that GLP-1 drugs

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.800
may increase the odds
of pancreatitis

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.480
as much as six-fold.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.560
This led some investigators
to conclude

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.280
that the balance of evidence
suggests an association

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.360
between the use
of GLP-1 based therapies

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.000
and acute pancreatitis.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.480
The major concern
is not pancreatitis, though.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:00.960
Acute pancreatitis is
unpleasant enough,

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.200
but the major concern is
subclinical, asymptomatic

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.880
inflammation of the pancreas,

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.960
because inflammation
of the pancreas

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.920
is well known to predispose
to pancreatic cancer,

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.480
which is one of the deadliest
forms of cancer.

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:18.240
And some of the rats did show
potentially premalignant changes

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:20.400
in their pancreases
on these drugs.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:23.200
The concern is that
the pro-proliferative actions

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:26.080
of GLP-1 could take
premalignant lesions

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:30.240
and accelerate their progression
towards cancer.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.640
Remember how these drugs
were modeled off a compound

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:35.760
found in Gila monster saliva?

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:39.360
Few have paused to wonder why
they would produce it.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.120
The answer is that
the Gila monster

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.600
is a desert lizard that goes
for weeks or even months

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.920
between meals
and conserves energy

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.160
during those intervals
by shrinking

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.960
its digestive tract,
including its pancreas.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.960
So, when it finally does eat,
it needs a way

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:56.320
to rapidly proliferate
its tissues.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.640
After reviewing thousands
of pages of documents

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.200
obtained through
freedom of information requests,

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.280
a British Medical Journal
investigation

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:06.720
unearthed unpublished data
from animal and human studies

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.760
that point to pathological
changes in the pancreas,

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:11.440
including attempts
by drug companies

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.520
to suppress scientific debate

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.680
by withholding
important safety data

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.520
from the public.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.840
Why have the companies been
so slow to respond

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:21.280
to this threat?

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:23.920
Because of
the "three monkey paradigm,"

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:26.720
which operates as follows.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.400
Companies are
legally responsible

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.040
for monitoring the safety
of their own products,

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:33.120
but obviously can’t be
held responsible

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.560
for tackling a safety concern
that does not exist.

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:39.520
A concern that can be
plausibly doubted or denied

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:42.000
carries no legal liability,

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.240
whereas one that gives rise
to serious consideration

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.720
leaves the door wide open
to lawsuits.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:49.760
Thus, inviting companies
to monitor the safety

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:52.000
of their own products
provides them

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.080
with the strongest
possible incentive

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.760
for failing to do so,

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.880
an instance of the law
of unintended consequences.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.640
The three monkeys,
who neither hear

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.240
nor see nor speak,

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.640
have been allowed to flourish
at the heart of our system

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.880
for protecting the public.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:08.560
"After careful reflection,"

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.960
wrote a professor of medicine
at the Mayo Clinic,

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.080
"most patients and clinicians
may opt to avoid

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.480
GLP-1 based drugs
or at least avoid using them

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.800
for a prolonged
period of time."

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:22.320
And this was all before
this pivotal study came out,

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:25.920
where researchers obtained
transplant-quality pancreases

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.520
from, like, accident victims

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.480
who had been taking GLP-1 drugs
for at least a year

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:31.920
before they died,

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:36.240
and every single pancreas
showed abnormalities,

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:40.000
marked enlargement, dysplasia,
and even a few little tumors.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:44.000
This was all discovered
more than a decade ago, though.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.200
Where are we now?

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.800
It remains unclear
whether the use of GLP-1 drugs

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:52.160
is linked to an increased risk
of pancreatic cancer.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.160
But trials
would have to be enormous

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:55.560
to exclude an increased risk,

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:58.160
and unless the rules
change radically

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:00.000
by the time
they are to be reported,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.000
most of the data
will remain hidden

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.600
from independent scrutiny.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.800
And as one Johns Hopkins
drug safety researcher asked,

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:09.200
"The fundamental question is
who bears the burden

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.480
of the passage of time

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.760
while these debates
are settled?"

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:15.840
Thousands
of pancreatic cancer cases

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:19.600
have been reportedly tied
to GLP-1 drugs, like Ozempic,

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:21.760
based on the U.S. Food
and Drug Administration’s

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:24.320
Adverse Events Reporting System,

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:28.000
but adverse event databases
that rely on voluntary reporting

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:31.200
are limited by the potential
for reporting bias.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:33.280
That’s like the Centers
for Disease Control’s

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:34.560
VAERS database,

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:37.440
the Vaccine Adverse Events
Reporting System.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:39.040
During COVID,

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:42.480
the more states were inclined
to vote Republican,

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:45.120
the more likely their vaccine
recipients or clinicians

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.920
were to report
COVID vaccine side effects;

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:50.800
so, maybe there was some kind
of similar reporting bias

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:53.040
among those who submit
their pancreatic cancer

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.560
to the FDA?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.960
Either way, if there is
even a remote chance

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:59.200
that certain drugs
can have an impact

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.880
on cancer development
and progression,

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:06.080
then such risks
should not be taken lightly.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.640
But if you really don’t want
to get cancer,

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.360
then you really don’t want
to be overweight.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:13.200
Based on a study
following millions of people,

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:15.120
the longer you’re overweight
or obese,

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.720
the higher your apparent risk

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:19.440
of 18 different kinds of cancer.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:22.080
So, even if you cared
only about cancer,

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:25.840
might these drugs actually lower
your overall cancer risk

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:28.240
if they caused
enough weight loss?

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:31.520
A meta-analysis
of bariatric surgery studies

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.360
found that those
going under the knife

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.200
tend to lose so much weight

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.200
that they have
a significantly lower risk

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.000
of getting cancer

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.160
and appear to cut
their risk of dying from cancer

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:42.000
nearly in half.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.720
This modeling study suggests
that widespread usage

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:47.840
of these new-generation
weight-loss drugs, like Ozempic,

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:51.360
could prevent more than,
like, 1 out of 100 cancers

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.280
over the next 25 years.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:54.720
And that’s just cancer.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:57.200
Wouldn’t just
the cardiovascular benefits

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:01.470
of losing a lot of weight alone
outweigh any potential risks?

